.TH SYS_PROC_LIST 2 "March 2026" "Substrate" "System Calls Manual"
.SH NAME
sys_proc_list \- list active process IDs
.SH LIBRARY
System library (libsys, \-lsys)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <sys/sysinfo.h>
.PP
.BI "int sys_proc_list(pid_t *" pids ", size_t " count ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR sys_proc_list ()
returns active PIDs from the kernel process table.
.PP
If
.I pids
is NULL or
.I count
is 0, the call returns the total active process count without copying IDs.
Otherwise, up to
.I count
PIDs are written to
.IR pids .
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, returns either:
- total active process count (query mode), or
- number of PIDs copied.
.PP
On failure, a negative error value is returned by the current implementation.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EFAULT
Output buffer is invalid.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sys_proc_info (2),
.BR sys_proc_count (2),
.BR getpid (2)
